Date: Mon, 20 Apr 2026 21:22:13 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 2/8] Rebrand the OPENCODE wordmark + TUI logo to HIVEMIND

Replaces the two ASCII-art glyph sources in the opencode source tree
that the user sees: the static `wordmark` array used by the exit screen
(`cli/ui.ts`), and the `logo.left`/`logo.right` paired arrays used by
the home-screen `<Logo />` component (`cli/logo.ts`).

Replaces the work of the deprecated `opencode/plugins/branding.js` TUI
plugin with a native source-level patch.

The HIVEMIND art is taken from the original branding plugin (5 slash-
art lines). The wordmark is trimmed to 4 lines to match the existing
exit-message template that references `logo[0]..logo[3]`. The TUI
`<Logo />` component iterates `logo.left` so we put the full 5-line art
on the left and emit empty padding strings on the right; the existing
shadow-marker rendering still works on the empty strings (no-op).
---
 packages/opencode/src/cli/logo.ts | 14 ++++++++++++--
 packages/opencode/src/cli/ui.ts   |  8 ++++----
 2 files changed, 16 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

